  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 global tax landscape is defined by the crystallization of a post-multilateral order. The OECD's Pillar Two initiative has hit a wall of sovereign resistance, marked by U.S. withdrawal and widespread domestic carve-outs that neutralize the 'global minimum' concept. In its place, nations are pivoting to aggressive unilateralism: tariff-based industrial protectionism has become a permanent feature of trade policy, and fiscal strategy is increasingly centered on bespoke incentive regimes to capture mobile capital. Concurrently, tax authorities are shifting from compliance-by-reporting to compliance-by-design, with mandatory, structured e-invoicing ecosystems\u2014exemplified by Singapore's InvoiceNow\u2014now serving as the primary infrastructure for indirect tax enforcement.",
